  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 203 AM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nUpper level high pressure will remain situated across the \nsouthwest CONUS with ridging in place across the High Plains through \nthe week. However, a series of disturbances will move along across \nthe ridge, the first of which being a cold front late Monday night \ninto Tuesday. This will bring reprieve to the extreme heat, although \ntemperatures will still be quite warm with highs remaining in the \nlow to mid 90s for Tuesday through Friday, at this time should \nremain below any heat headline criteria. There will also be chances \nfor isolated to scattered thunderstorm chances Tuesday through \nThursday as disturbances move along the ridge, but any organized \nthunderstorm development looks low at this time, so no widespread \nprecipitation chance, but precipitation chances nonetheless. At\nthis time severe weather potential is low, but will continue to\nmonitor. As far as fire weather concerns in the long term, \nexpect additional low level moisture around the area keeping min\nRH values around 30 percent or higher mid-week to the end of \nthe week.",
